# Gameplay Review — Deprecated

This skill has been merged into `/competitor-lookup`.

**What changed**: The old approach scored games numerically across 8 dimensions (Art = 7/10, etc.).
The new approach collects descriptive intelligence — what the game actually is, how it feels,
what it offers — so you can understand the market rather than benchmark against it.

## Use instead

```
/competitor-lookup [genre]
```

This now collects all data in one step:
- Factual: Year, Revenue, Reviews, Team Size, Art Style
- Descriptive: Game Feel, Features, Scope, Content, Replayability

Saves to both an Excel file (`gameplay-review-[genre].xlsx`) and a genre-specific Google Sheets tab.

## Legacy data

Existing rows in the `📊 Quality Scores` tab (numeric scores) are still in the sheet.
New research goes to genre-specific tabs (`🏆 [genre-slug]`) with the updated schema.
